# The documentation trees are hand-formatted. Prettier is wrong for them beyond the
# decision records: it reflows embedded markdown inside a fence, and the record-header
# example in template_docs/adr/README.md is exactly that case. A create-adr record is
# worse: Prettier inserts a blank line after the heading and merges the `Status:` and
# `Classification:` lines, destroying the three-line header the format depends on.
# check_adr.py owns the record format; the rest of both trees is maintained by hand.
#
# The consequence is that nothing in these trees is machine-formatted, so the
# semantic-line-break rule is discipline rather than a gate. That rule, its exceptions,
# and its accepted cost are stated in template_docs/development-workflow.md; do not
# restate them here, or the two drift. The root documents (AGENTS.md, README.md,
# CHANGELOG.md) are still Prettier-formatted and still use proseWrap: 'never'.
